{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935431-clash-of-wills-and-ghouls","id":935431,"title":"Clash of Wills and Ghouls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-21T20:18:39-07:00","id":935431,"title":"Clash of Wills and Ghouls","content":"Does clash of wills involving a ghoul vs vampire even work? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vtr2e pg 297</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contests and Resistance: When a Discipline would be<br /> contested or resisted by one of the Kindred, the ghoul may not<br /> add his Discipline dots to his own roll. If he has any stage of<br /> blood bond to the vampire, the Discipline fails automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does a clash of wills count as a contest in this or only contested disciplines? I've been ruling the prior and thought I would make sure I've been doing it right since it came up when I was playing tonight rather than ST'ing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T03:31:20-07:00","id":935500,"title":"","content":"For that specific situation it's not a clash of wills. The situation spoken about there is where there's an opposed roll or a resisted one, rather than a power interacting with another power (so just using dominate on a vampire won't trigger a clash but clash of wills comes up when that vampire already has a dominate command on them which is contradictory to the one being placed). Contest in this situation is just where the dice pool of the discipline is attribute + skill + discipline vs attribute + supernatural tolerance (like the 4th dot of auspex where it is intelligence + socialize + auspex vs resolve + blood potency).<br /> <br /> Basically a clash of wills will only occur when 2 powers are interfering and is a way to determine which power comes out on top, not just as a general rule for when powers are used on supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> That said I think I remember reading that without a full template (like vampire, mage, or whatever) or being a non-playable being (like a spirit or horror) you don't get to clash of wills and are just treated as automatically losing when going up against a full template or non-playable being (so a ghoul or wolf-blooded will always lose a clash against a vampire or mage or spirit, but can clash against ghouls or wolf-blooded or proximi etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T04:25:53-07:00","id":935514,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that the side bar should apply to Clash of Wills as well. It seems to follow the spirit of the rules to rule so. Ghouls are servants and slaves, not masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:46:10-07:00","id":935575,"title":"","content":"<i> &quot; All characters using conflicting powers enter a contested<br /> roll-off, each using a pool of his Blood Potency plus his dots in<br /> the Discipline.<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills can apply to other supernatural creatures, as<br /> well. The traits involved depend on the creature and will be<br /> elaborated upon in later books. &quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> I am conflicted on the matter as ^^ that is what is stated in clash of wills. It is Contested, but it also said that all can do it, not all except.. But Fumas does have a point they arent a full template. <br /> <br /> Obviously a ghoul doesnt have BP so they would add their discipline dots only (maybe ) which makes them more likely to fail, which follows the theme of not as good as a vampire.. or is it 0 BP + 0 Dots = 0 dice? ( chance die )<br /> <br /> So say a ghoul a vampire both want to go first with Celerity. Do they clash?<br /> A ghoul and a vampire both give John Doe a dominate command, one to sit and and one to stand. Do they Clash?<br /> <br /> Or is this just for.. I am going to go dominate Vampire X over there. I subtract my dots from my pool. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:06:56-07:00","id":935606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935431-clash-of-wills-and-ghouls?p=935500#post935500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I think I remember reading that without a full template (like vampire, mage, or whatever) or being a non-playable being (like a spirit or horror) you don't get to clash of wills and are just treated as automatically losing when going up against a full template or non-playable being (so a ghoul or wolf-blooded will always lose a clash against a vampire or mage or spirit, but can clash against ghouls or wolf-blooded or proximi etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were the case then the rules would have just said flat out that a ghoul's disciplines fail against a vampire target with no mention of invoking a clash of wills as was the case in 1st edition. But now a ghoul can successfully use powers against other vampires because, quite frequently, the use of vampiric disciplines on a target are unresistable. If they're going to reinforce the notion that ghouls are inferior to vampires without completely invalidating the effectiveness of discipline use for both parties, they are going to have to find a way to make disciplines less useful to ghouls against a vampire target. So IF a vampire gets the opportunity to contest or resist a ghoul's discipline use, the ghoul will be at diminished capacity due to modified resist checks or penalized contested rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-22-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:18:54-07:00","id":935642,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ghouls can engage in a Clash of Wills. They're at a disadvantage, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:13:06-07:00","id":935662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935431-clash-of-wills-and-ghouls?p=935642#post935642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, ghouls can engage in a Clash of Wills. They're at a disadvantage, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Could you clarify just a little more?<br /> <br /> Do they get 0 BP + 0 Discipline to = Chance die<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do they get 0BP + Discipline 1-5 to equal 1-5 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:58:49-07:00","id":936105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935431-clash-of-wills-and-ghouls?p=935662#post935662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks! Could you clarify just a little more?<br /> <br /> Do they get 0 BP + 0 Discipline to = Chance die<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do they get 0BP + Discipline 1-5 to equal 1-5 ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It'd be 0 + discipline dots, they have 0 in a power stat but the not counting discipline dots in the roll is only for contested discipline rolls against vampires, not clashes of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:02:38-07:00","id":936108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935431-clash-of-wills-and-ghouls?p=936105#post936105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be 0 + discipline dots, they have 0 in a power stat but the not counting discipline dots in the roll is only for contested discipline rolls against vampires, not clashes of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is what I thought it would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}